---
import Site from '../layouts/Site.astro';
import CodeExample from '../components/CodeExample.astro';
import source from '../../examples/effects.ash?raw';
---
<Site title="Ash" description="Explore Ash: typed functional programming, explicit effects, and scoped resources. Discover the language, try a short tour, and follow its development.">
  <div class="home" data-pagefind-body>
    <div class="intro-line"><p class="eyebrow">The Ash programming language</p><a class="status-pill" href="/status/"><span aria-hidden="true"></span>In active development <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
    <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
      <div class="hero-copy"><h1 id="hero-title">Express the program.<br /><em>Understand</em><br />its boundaries.</h1><p class="hero-description">Typed functional programming with explicit effects and scoped resources. A small language exploring a bigger connection between code and reasoning.</p><div class="hero-actions"><a class="button primary" href="/learn/tour/">Take the language tour <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="text-link" href="/discover/">Why Ash? <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div><p class="hero-footnote">For curious programmers. Open to deeper questions.</p></div>
      <div class="hero-example"><div class="example-caption"><span>01 / A FIRST LOOK</span><span>Effects, made explicit</span></div><CodeExample source={source} filename="effects.ash" output="42 : Int" /><p class="example-explanation">The calculation asks for a value.<br />The handler decides how to answer.</p><a class="text-link" href="/learn/tour/#effects-and-handlers">Walk through this program <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div>
    </section>
    <section class="principles" aria-labelledby="principles-title"><div class="section-intro"><p class="eyebrow">A few starting points</p><h2 id="principles-title">Small pieces.<br />Explicit relationships.</h2><a class="text-link" href="/discover/">Meet the language →</a></div><div class="principle-list"><div><span class="item-number">01</span><div><h3>Let data describe the problem.</h3><p>Nominal data types, pattern matching, and checked coverage make the possible cases visible.</p></div></div><div><span class="item-number">02</span><div><h3>Say what a computation can request.</h3><p>Effect rows describe requests. Lexical handlers provide their meaning in the surrounding program.</p></div></div><div><span class="item-number">03</span><div><h3>Keep resource access in scope.</h3><p>Scoped resources make ownership boundaries part of checking, including captured access.</p></div></div></div></section>
    <section class="paths" aria-labelledby="paths-title"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Choose your next step</p><h2 id="paths-title">There’s more than one way in.</h2></div><p>Start with a program.<br />Follow the questions that matter to you.</p></div><div class="path-grid"><a class="path-card" href="/learn/tour/"><span class="eyebrow">Explore</span><h3>I already write code.</h3><p>Get a feel for Ash through a short tour of functions, data, and effects.</p><span class="path-cta">Take the tour <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></span></a><a class="path-card" href="/learn/#new-to-programming"><span class="eyebrow">Learn</span><h3>I want to learn.</h3><p>Find a guided route, build a first program, and work through examples.</p><span class="path-cta">Find your starting point <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></span></a><a class="path-card" href="/contribute/"><span class="eyebrow">Investigate</span><h3>I want to go deeper.</h3><p>Read the specification, examine the design, or help shape what comes next.</p><span class="path-cta">Research & contribute <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></span></a></div></section>
    <section class="honest-status" aria-labelledby="status-title"><div><p class="eyebrow">Where things stand</p><h2 id="status-title">A working language.<br />An open direction.</h2></div><div><p>Ash has an executable implementation and a language specification. Its broader goal—bringing programs, properties, and evidence into one language—is still a direction of research.</p><a class="text-link" href="/status/">What works today, and what doesn’t <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></section>
    <section class="latest-update"><p class="eyebrow">From the project</p><a href="/updates/first-version/"><time datetime="2026-10-18">18 October 2026</time><h2>A public home for an evolving language.</h2><span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="text-link" href="/updates/">All updates →</a></section>
  </div>
</Site>
